<BaseLayout
  title="About HKML — Hong Kong Machine Learning"
  description="HKML is Hong Kong’s open community for substantive exchange across AI, machine learning, data science, and quantitative research."
  canonicalPath="/about/"
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="kicker">About HKML</p>
      <h1>Technical depth.<br />Open exchange.</h1>
      <p>A community where researchers, practitioners, students, and founders can share work in progress, challenge ideas, and build lasting connections.</p>
    </div>
  </header>
  <section class="section section-white">
    <div class="container about-grid">
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="kicker">Why we meet</p>
        <h2>A modern salon for machine learning.</h2>
        <p>HKML brings together people working across academia, industry, startups, and quantitative research. Our meetups are designed for substantial ideas without unnecessary ceremony: clear talks, direct questions, and time to continue the conversation.</p>
        <p>Each gathering usually combines focused presentations with shorter pitches and informal networking. The topics move with the field, but the goal stays constant—help useful ideas and thoughtful people find each other.</p>
        <a class="button button-primary" href="https://www.meetup.com/hong-kong-machine-learning-meetup/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Meet the community <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="principles">
        <div class="principle"><strong>Substance first</strong><p>Technical ideas explained clearly, with enough space for nuance and honest questions.</p></div>
        <div class="principle"><strong>Academia meets industry</strong><p>Research, production experience, and entrepreneurial practice belong in the same room.</p></div>
        <div class="principle"><strong>Open by design</strong><p>Experienced practitioners and people entering the field are equally welcome to participate.</p></div>
        <div class="principle"><strong>Made in Hong Kong</strong><p>Rooted in the city and connected to the wider machine-learning community.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
